        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(ui): redesign Settings About with Clawd hero and community links",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Settings → About page was a bare build-identity table: version, commit, branch, build date, and the connected Gateway version. It had no product identity and no way to reach the project's community surfaces — unlike the native macOS and iOS About screens, which both link Website, Docs, GitHub, and Discord. Users looking for \"where do I get help / file an issue / read the changelog\" had nothing to click.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBring the Control UI About page up to (and past) the native About screens:\n\n- **Clawd hero**: the same canonical crimson lobster as the chat welcome screen, rendered large with ambient breathe/blink and a periodic claw wave. Clicking (or keyboard-activating) Clawd replays the wave. All motion is disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n- **Product identity**: OpenClaw name, tagline (from the README), and a version pill.\n- **Community links**: Website, Docs, GitHub, Discord, Changelog — matching the native About screens (`AboutSettings.swift`, `SettingsProTabSections.swift`) and the sidebar agent menu's docs-first policy. New `github`/`discord` brand icons added to the shared icon set.\n- **License footer**: `© 2026 OpenClaw Foundation — MIT License.`, same as native.\n\nThe existing build-identity card (version / commit+copy / branch / built / connected Gateway version) is kept unchanged below the hero — that data still matters for support.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSettings → About now shows a friendly product identity with one-click access to Website, Docs, GitHub, Discord, and the Changelog, in light/dark and down to mobile widths. No behavior change for the build-identity details or the commit copy button.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Screenshots (light, dark, mobile): see comment below.\n- Unit tests: hero identity/links/rel/target, poke wave callback, wave-class toggling (`ui/src/pages/about/view.test.ts`).\n- Browser layout test updated for new props (`ui/src/pages/about/view.browser.test.ts`).\n- E2E (mock gateway): hero name + version pill, GitHub/Discord hrefs, `target=\"_blank\"` + `noopener`, poke wave class, license footer, plus all pre-existing About assertions (`ui/src/e2e/about.e2e.test.ts`).\n- Gates: `format:check`, `ui:i18n:check`, `tsgo:ui`, `tsgo:test:ui`, oxlint, and the About unit/browser/e2e suites — run on Testbox/Crabbox (run IDs in PR comment).\n",
        "branch": "claude/about-screen-redesign-044fb4",
